# Kingdom: Project Rules

## Stack
- Vite + TypeScript + Phaser 3
- Browser game, no backend
- Run: `npm run dev`
- Deploys to GitHub Pages on push to main (.github/workflows/deploy.yml)

## Structure (do not explore to confirm this, trust it)
- src/main.ts: Phaser game config and boot (loads MapScene)
- src/world/: game data and logic only, no Phaser imports
  - tile.ts: Tile type (terrain, owner, city, improvement, road, city hp/walls/shield), terrain rules, yields, claim costs
  - map.ts: WorldMap, map generation, neighbors, raiseHeight/lowerHeight
  - units.ts: unit types/stats (builder, settler, swordsman, archer, knight), training, builder jobs, movement costs, reachable()
  - game.ts: GameState: players, gold/food/stone, turns, claim, recruit/train/move/jobs, settlers, combat (attackPreview/attack), city capture, idle-unit check/hold, win checks, DIFFICULTY table
  - ai.ts: rival AI (troops, builders, settlers, recruiting, land). Uses only public GameState methods, same rules as the human
  - save.ts: autosave/load to localStorage (key kingdom-save-v3)
- src/scenes/: rendering and input only
  - MapScene.ts: draws hexes, roads, buildings, unit tokens with drawn icons, borders, city bars, claim zone; selection, movement, attack targets, modes, camera, end-of-turn idle check; autosaves after every redraw
  - Hud.ts: DOM overlay (collapsible stats/help/selection panels, mode bar, tooltip, idle-unit prompt, game over)
  - Menu.ts: start screen (map size, rivals, difficulty, free building, continue)
- src/game/ and the other files in src/scenes/ are old unused stubs

## Behavior rules
- Do NOT run ls, find, or read files to explore the project unless I ask or a file I mention is missing.
- Only touch files related to the current request.
- Do one step at a time. Do not add features I didn't ask for.
- Do not plan the full implementation in your head first. Write the files, then fix issues.
- Keep world logic out of scenes. Scenes read from world, never the other way around.
- Scenes change the world only through GameState methods (perform, recruit, moveUnit, doJob, foundCity, attack, setHold, endTurn).
- The AI must play by the same rules: only call public GameState methods from ai.ts, never edit tiles/units directly.
- If you add new state to GameState, Tile, Unit or GameOptions, add it to save.ts too (with a default for old saves).
- After changes, tell me what changed in 1-3 lines and how to test it.

## Game rules (current)
- Pointy-top hexes, odd rows shifted right (odd-r offset). Sizes: small 20x14, medium 30x20, large 44x30, huge 60x40
- Height 0-5: 0 water, 1 sand, 2-3 grass, 4 hills, 5 mountain
- Players: You (blue) + 0-3 AI rivals. 0 rivals = sandbox (no win conditions, no troops)
- Difficulty (DIFFICULTY in game.ts, default Easy):
  - Easy: AI 70% income, max 3 troops, attacks from turn 45, walls level 1, can't win by land share
  - Normal: 100% income, max 8 troops, attacks from turn 22 with 4+ troops, walls level 2
  - Hard: 125% income, max 14 troops, attacks from turn 14, counters your troop types, focuses weak targets, retreats wounded units, only marches on you
- Gold per turn: tile yield (sand/grass 1, hills 2, mountain 0) + city 3 + capital 5
- Food is supply: capital 3, city 2, farm 3. Units (and units in training) use food
- Stone: mines give 2/turn, pays for walls
- Builder (15g, instant, 2 moves): one job per turn on own land: farm, mine, road, walls (on a city: 10/20/30 stone + 5g, +40 shield per level, max 3), raise/lower its tile or a neighbor
- Settler (10g + 10g per city owned, 3 turns): founds a city on unclaimed or own land, 3+ hexes from any city; consumed. Settlers are the only way to found cities
- Claim: buy UNOWNED land only, bordering yours, within 3 hexes (CLAIM_RADIUS) of one of your cities. Claim mode dims everything outside the zone and outlines it in yellow. Price +8% per tile bought. Owned land can never be claimed: the only way to take it is to capture the city
- City HP 100, capital 150. Shield absorbs damage first. Both regen 10/turn unless enemy troops within 2 hexes
- Troops: Swordsman (25g, 2 turns, 30hp, atk 8, beats Archer), Archer (30g, 2 turns, 20hp, atk 7, range 2, no return fire, beats Knight), Knight (45g, 3 turns, 2 food, 35hp, atk 10, 4 moves, beats Swordsman, half damage vs walls)
- Combat: one attack per turn, ends movement. Strong-vs = 1.5x. Hills 0.8 / mountain 0.7 / own city 0.75 damage taken. Melee defenders hit back at 50%. Cities hit melee attackers back (4 + 2 per wall level). Troops deal 1.5x to cities
- Capture: city at 0 HP + Swordsman/Knight moves in. Captor gets the city and the loser's land closer to it than to their other cities. Capturing a capital eliminates that player (all their land to captor)
- Units heal 5/turn at home, 2 elsewhere
- End turn: if any of your units haven't moved/acted (and aren't on Hold), a prompt offers Show me / Hold them all / End turn anyway. H toggles Hold on a unit; moving or acting clears it
- Move costs: grass/sand 1, hills 2, mountain 3, road-to-road 0.5. Enemy cities block movement until destroyed
- Win: take every rival capital or hold 60% of land (rivals on Easy can't win by land)

## Roadmap
1. DONE builders, food, stone, farms, mines, roads, settlers
2. DONE city HP + walls
3. DONE troops, combat, capture
4. DONE AI uses builders (farms, mines, walls), troops (defend, attack, capture), settlers; Easy/Normal/Hard
5. DONE first balance pass (AI troop mix, Easy has no AI land win)
6. DONE unit icons, end-of-turn idle check, claim radius 3 with zone outline

## Open ideas (not started)
- Terraforming: 2-hex builder reach and/or a "Shape land" brush in sandbox/free-build
- Delete old stubs in src/game/ and unused src/scenes/ files (they break `npm run build`)
